    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d773-a1">

                <pb facs="0728" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg630"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Long to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March 12,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith a copy
                    of a letter from the commanding officer of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wheeling</hi>, wherein he expresses his appreciation of the unreserved
                    kindness <pb facs="0729" n="631" xml:id="pg631"/> of the British officers and
                    men at the time of an explosion on board the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wheeling</hi>, at Hongkong, China.</p>
                <p>The Department requests that, if compatible with the views of the State
                    Department, this appreciation of the kindness shown be conveyed to the British
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John D. Long</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
